# Snagset — environment.
#
# GENERATED from the server's configuration registry with each release.
# Do not edit by hand.
#
# Copy to apps/server/.env and uncomment what you need. Everything here is
# commented out on purpose — the defaults are a working install.

# ── The only one you must set ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres 14+. Supabase, Neon, RDS, or a local install — any of them. A
# POOLED string is fine and is what a managed provider hands you: on
# Supabase, the session pooler (port 5432) for a Node process and the
# transaction pooler (6543) on serverless — never the IPv6-only direct
# string on a host without IPv6. TLS is on for any non-local host unless
# SNAGSET_DATABASE_SSL says otherwise. Quote it: `&` ends a shell line.
DATABASE_URL="postgres://user:password@host:5432/snagset"

# ── First run, with no browser (optional but recommended) ──────────────
# Set these and the instance claims itself on boot: owner, first project,
# and the origins allowed to talk to it. No claim URL to click, which is
# what makes an install reproducible and scriptable.
#
# The password is a FILE, never an inline variable — an env var is visible
# in /proc, in `docker inspect` and in any crash report that dumps the
# environment. A mounted secret has its own lifetime and permissions.
#
# Both the email and the file must be set, or neither. All of it is IGNORED
# once an org exists, so it is safe to leave in place across redeploys.
# SNAGSET_BOOTSTRAP_OWNER_EMAIL=
# e.g. /run/secrets/snagset-owner-password (12 chars minimum, trimmed)
# SNAGSET_BOOTSTRAP_OWNER_PASSWORD_FILE=
# SNAGSET_BOOTSTRAP_PROJECT_NAME=
# comma-separated; scheme required, port included: https://staging.acme.com,http://localhost:3000,https://*.acme.com
# SNAGSET_BOOTSTRAP_PROJECT_ORIGINS=

# ── Where the server thinks it lives ───────────────────────────────────
# Public origin. Review links and the claim URL are built from it.
# SNAGSET_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
# SNAGSET_PORT=8080
# SNAGSET_BIND_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0

# ── Email (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ONE variable; its scheme picks the transport. Unset means notifications
# are off and the dashboard says so — nothing is queued.
#
#   resend://re_your_api_key        a provider owns SPF/DKIM/DMARC
#   smtp://user:pass@host:587       your own mail server (STARTTLS)
#   smtps://user:pass@host:465      your own mail server (implicit TLS)
#
# With Resend the sending DOMAIN must be verified at resend.com/domains
# before it will accept mail from SNAGSET_MAIL_FROM.
# SNAGSET_MAIL_URL=
# SNAGSET_MAIL_FROM=
#
# How the owner hears about new comments: `digest` (the default) is at most
# one email a day, after midnight UTC, grouped by site; `each` is one email
# per comment. Nobody is mailed about a comment they wrote themselves.
# SNAGSET_MAIL_NOTIFY=digest

# ── Screenshots and uploads (optional) ─────────────────────────────────
# Any S3-compatible bucket: DigitalOcean Spaces, Cloudflare R2, MinIO, AWS.
# Set all four or none — a partial set is a boot failure naming what is
# missing, rather than a silent drop to annotation mode.
#
# The server PROBES these at boot (write, read, delete of one small object)
# and warns loudly if they do not work, because credentials that are merely
# well-formed are the ones that fail on the first screenshot, in front of a
# reviewer, an hour later.
# https://ams3.digitaloceanspaces.com, https://<account>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# SNAGSET_STORAGE_S3_ENDPOINT=
# SNAGSET_STORAGE_S3_BUCKET=
# auto suits R2; Spaces wants ams3/nyc3/…; AWS wants the real one
# SNAGSET_STORAGE_S3_REGION=auto
# On DigitalOcean this is the SHORT value (~20 chars, DO00…)
# SNAGSET_STORAGE_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# …and this is the long one (~43 chars) beside it
# SNAGSET_STORAGE_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Or connect one at runtime instead, without a redeploy — credentials are
# encrypted in the database, and the environment wins if both are present:
#
#   snagset storage status
#   echo "$SECRET" | snagset storage connect \
#     https://ams3.digitaloceanspaces.com my-bucket DO00XXXXXXXX - ams3
#
# With no bucket at all the product runs in annotation mode: comments work,
# and the widget is TOLD screenshots are unavailable rather than offered one
# that fails (A9b).

# ── Secrets at rest (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Left unset, the server generates a key into SNAGSET_DATA_DIR on first
# boot and tells you to back it up. Set it explicitly on a platform with
# no writable disk.
# SNAGSET_SECRET_KEY=
# SNAGSET_DATA_DIR=./.snagset

# ── Everything else ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 65 further variables are registered — rate limits, retention windows,
# proxy trust, OAuth apps, storage ceilings; `npx snagset env` lists them all.
# None is required.
